WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.588
"House of the Dragon" is full of new faces,
and not all of them used to belong to "The Doctor."

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:08.516
Here's where else you've seen the talented
cast.

00:00:08.516 --> 00:00:13.750
Someone must always sit on the Iron Throne,
and at the start of "House of the Dragon,"

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:19.970
that responsibility falls to King Viserys
Targaryen, played by veteran actor Paddy Considine.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:25.300
King Viserys is described in HBO's official
promotions for the series as a "good man,"

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.180
setting him miles apart from the "Game of
Thrones" character who later bears his name.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.450
Outside of Westeros, Considine has had a long
and varied career in both film and television.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:41.720
A versatile and lauded performer, he's equally
well known for indie films like "Dead Man's

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.403
Shoes" and "In America" and big-budget blockbusters
like "The Bourne Ultimatum."

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.920
"I can't think.

00:00:49.788 --> 00:00:50.581
I can't laugh.

00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:51.373
I can't cry.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.919
I can't feel!"

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.804
He's also collaborated with Simon Pegg and
Nick Frost on "Hot Fuzz" and "The World's End."

00:01:00.804 --> 00:01:06.037
Considine's other major TV roles include Claude
Bolton in the Stephen King adaptation "The

00:01:06.037 --> 00:01:11.464
Outsider," and the despicable Father John
Hughes in the British crime saga "Peaky Blinders."

00:01:11.464 --> 00:01:16.400
Though the Targaryens are at the center of
"House of the Dragon," they're far from the

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.640
only great house in Westeros with a stake
in the game.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.390
One of the other major players is House Hightower
— a family that doesn't play an especially

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:30.360
major role in "Game of Thrones," but which
has a long and storied history on the continent.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.710
One of the main characters in "House of the
Dragon" is Alicent Hightower, daughter of

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.650
Ser Otto Hightower, the Hand of the King.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.640
Teenage Alicent is played by newcomer Emily
Carey.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.841
Alicent Hightower is brought to life as an
adult by English actor Olivia Cooke, a young

00:01:45.841 --> 00:01:50.290
star who's nonetheless accrued a lot of notable
credits in her career.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.290
"Ruben?

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.000
You hurt yourself?

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.610
You hurt me.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.939
I'll hurt myself too.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:58.750
I'll hurt myself too."

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:03.110
Cooke first rose to prominence starring in
a couple of BBC miniseries, including "The

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:07.159
Secret of Crickley Hall" — alongside "Game
of Thrones" star Maisie Williams.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:13.120
She's also plied her trade in the Alfred Hitchcock-inspired
series "Bates Motel" and the ITV historical

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.450
drama "Vanity Fair."

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:20.129
On the big screen, Cooke has appeared in films
like "Sound of Metal" and Steven Spielberg's "Ready Player One."

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:27.079
What would "A Song of Ice and Fire" be without
a few cool, enigmatic rogue warrior types?

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:31.879
That's the archetype that Lord Corlys Velaryon
falls into in "House of the Dragon," though

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:34.590
you'd be wrong to write him off as simply
a trope.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:39.489
Viewed in his day as the best sea captain
in all of Westeros, Corlys hails from a family

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:42.150
nearly as prestigious as House Targaryen.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:46.980
A key part of the royal court and a respected
ruler in his own right, the Sea Snake isn't

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.247
a man to be trifled with.

00:02:51.241 --> 00:02:52.682
"Four ships have now been lost!

00:02:53.249 --> 00:02:54.629
The last one was flying my banner."

00:02:54.629 --> 00:02:59.319
You might not immediately recognize the name
Steve Toussaint — but you've almost certainly

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:01.139
seen him in something.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:05.659
The Hollywood veteran has had a long career,
with credits that range from genre fare like

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:10.340
"Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time" to serious
dramas on the stage and screen.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.590
Toussaint is most prolific on television,
though, with roles in "The Knock," "Inspector

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.793
Lewis," and Netflix's "Pine Gap."

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:22.300
At the center of the drama in "House of the
Dragon" is Prince Daemon Targaryen, played

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.180
by British star Matt Smith.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:29.530
The younger brother of King Viserys and uncle
to Princess Rhaenyra, Daemon is a dragonrider,

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:33.861
warrior, and all-around major player in the
politics of the continent.

00:03:33.861 --> 00:03:38.400
A complicated figure to say the least, he
played a major role in the Dance of the Dragons

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.680
and the preceding political turmoil, in part
because of his own desire for power.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:49.540
Most fans of sci-fi and fantasy television
will instantly recognize Smith as the Eleventh

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:55.790
Doctor in "Doctor Who," a role he played for
three seasons from 2010 to 2013 and for which

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.109
he gained widespread acclaim.

00:03:58.109 --> 00:03:59.695
"How very skinny.

00:04:00.226 --> 00:04:01.917
That is proper skinny.

00:04:02.059 --> 00:04:03.726
I've never seen him from the outside."

00:04:03.815 --> 00:04:08.779
Fans of historical dramas may know Smith better
for his role as Prince Philip in Netflix's

00:04:08.779 --> 00:04:13.469
"The Crown" — a performance that earned
him a Primetime Emmy nomination in 2018.

00:04:13.469 --> 00:04:18.590
On the big screen, Smith is known for roles
like Jack in Edgar Wright's "Last Night in

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.221
Soho," Alex in "Terminator Genisys," and the
villainous Milo in "Morbius."

00:04:23.306 --> 00:04:29.440
The main action of "House of the Dragon" precedes
and involves the Dance of the Dragons, a civil

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.780
war of sorts fought between different Targaryen
claimants to the Iron Throne.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:39.900
One of those claimants is Princess Rhaenyra
Targaryen, played as an adult by Emma D'Arcy .

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.950
An actor equally at home on the stage and
the screen, D'Arcy started out in various

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:48.610
live theater productions in the U.K. before
landing some TV and film roles.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:53.350
D'Arcy appeared in the 2020 British comedy
"Misbehaviour," the BBC drama "Baptiste" and

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.700
the ITV comedy drama "Wild Bill," just to
name a few roles.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.260
The role of Rhaenyra in "House of the Dragon"
is undoubtedly D'Arcy's highest-profile role

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:08.208
to date — one shared by Australian newcomer
Milly Alcock, who plays the Princess as a 15-year-old

00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:14.350
Every "Game of Thrones" fan knows what an
important (and often dangerous) position the

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.540
Hand of the King is in Westeros.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:21.310
Depending on the current monarch of the land,
the Hand may wind up being the true ruler

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.040
behind the scenes.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:28.500
Like his father before him, King Viserys Targaryen
relies on Otto Hightower as his Hand, played

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.670
in "House of the Dragon" by Rhys Ifans.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:36.440
A longstanding member of the royal court and
a man of nearly impeccable reputation, Otto

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.800
is also the father of Alicent Hightower — a
role that ends up pulling him even further

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.330
into the messy family politics of the Targaryens.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:49.260
A Welsh actor and longtime star of the screen,
Ifans is probably best known for his roles

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:50.139
in "Notting Hill" …

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:51.405
"C'mon.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.790
Open up.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.123
This is me...

00:05:57.718 --> 00:05:58.532
Spiky." 

00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:04.690
… the "Harry Potter" franchise, and as Dr.
Curt Connors (aka the Lizard) in "The Amazing Spider-Man."

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:09.190
Ifans has also had a number of prominent television
roles, including playing Sherlock Holmes'

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:12.650
older brother Mycroft in the CBS crime procedural
"Elementary."

00:06:12.989 --> 00:06:19.540
Dragonrider, overlooked heir, and wife to
the Sea Snake Corlys Velaryon, Princess Rhaenys

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.900
Targaryen occupies a unique role in the royal
court of Westeros.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:28.820
Rhaenys carries the less-than-proud nickname
of the Queen who Never Was — a reference

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:35.370
to her being passed up as successor to King
Jaehaerys I in favor of her cousin Viserys.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:40.280
Being denied the Iron Throne does little to
curb Princess Rhaenys' influence and drive,

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:44.200
however, and she forms a fearsome couple with
her seafaring husband.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.520
Rhaenys is played by TV stalwart Eve Best
in "House of the Dragon."

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.770
Best is probably most recognizable for her
longstanding role as Dr. Eleanor O'Hara in

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:58.190
"Nurse Jackie," and for her supporting performance
as Wallis Simpson in "The King's Speech."

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:02.680
More recently, she's appeared in the BBC miniseries
"The Honorable Woman," and Netflix's teen

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.307
fantasy show "Fate: The Winx Saga."

00:07:05.307 --> 00:07:11.480
Initially an outsider in the court of King
Viserys Targaryen, Mysaria isn't even a native of Westeros.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:17.330
And yet, she eventually rises to become what
HBO calls "the most trusted — and most unlikely

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.760
— ally of Prince Daemon Targaryen."

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:25.080
Mysaria is brought to life by Sonoya Mizuno,
an actor arguably known best for her many

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.820
collaborations with sci-fi auteur Alex Garland.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:34.410
Mizuno has featured in several of Garland's
projects, including "Ex Machina" and the cosmic

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.490
horror masterpiece "Annihilation."

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:41.820
Her other film credits include "Crazy Rich
Asians," "Beauty and the Beast," and "La La Land."

00:07:41.899 --> 00:07:48.400
Neither a Lord nor a ruler, Ser Criston Cole
might seem at first like the odd man out in

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.430
the main cast of "House of the Dragon."

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:56.070
Being common-born, he's not exactly overflowing
with riches or power, but he manages to defeat

00:07:56.070 --> 00:08:02.360
Daemon Targaryen in combat in the premiere
episode, and make a strong impression on Princess Rhaenyra.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:06.820
Just as Criston Cole is a bit of an unknown
quantity in "House of the Dragon," so too

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:10.900
is actor Fabien Frankel, the least established
star in the main cast.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:15.620
A graduate of the Royal Academy of Dramatic
Art and the London Academy of Music and Dramatic

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:20.450
Art, Frankel got his big break in the BBC
One miniseries "The Serpent," which tells

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:24.280
the terrifying real-life story of a French
serial killer.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:29.800
He also appeared in the 2019 romantic comedy
"Last Christmas," alongside "Game of Thrones"

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.800
star Emilia Clarke.

00:08:30.932 --> 00:08:35.099
Where would a king of Westeros be without
his Kingsguard?

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:39.629
The white-cloaked guardians of the royal family
have always played a key role in "A Song of

00:08:39.629 --> 00:08:43.649
Ice and Fire," and that tradition continues
in "House of the Dragon."

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:48.260
As Lord Commander of the Kingsguard during
the reign of King Viserys Targaryen, Ser Harrold

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.720
Westerling has a lot on his plate.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:55.230
"House of the Dragon" sets him in a tumultuous
time for the family he's sworn to protect,

00:08:55.230 --> 00:09:00.220
but he carries himself with dignity and professionalism
nonetheless.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.550
Fans of the fantasy genre should be well acquainted
with Graham McTavish, the actor responsible

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:06.930
for embodying Ser Harrold in "House of the
Dragon."

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:12.079
He appears in all three of Peter Jackson's
"The Hobbit" films, as well as the Starz time-travel

00:09:12.079 --> 00:09:14.050
fantasy epic "Outlander."

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.253
"It's fiction.

00:09:16.253 --> 00:09:17.644
Outlander's fiction."

00:09:17.644 --> 00:09:22.990
Just as comfortable in a voice booth, McTavish
has lent his vocal talents to a number of

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:28.999
video games and animated series and films,
including Dracula in Netflix's critically-acclaimed

00:09:28.999 --> 00:09:30.860
"Castlevania" series.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:36.339
That all barely even scratches the surface
of McTavish's career, which also includes

00:09:36.339 --> 00:09:41.719
credits like the Saint of Killers in "Preacher,"
among many other smaller roles.

00:09:41.833 --> 00:09:45.931
While the family may not be too important
during the events of "Game of Thrones," one

00:09:45.931 --> 00:09:52.230
particular member of House Beesbury — Lord
Lyman — plays a key role in "House of the Dragon."

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:56.390
As an ally of the Hightowers and the Master
of Coin on King Viserys' Small Council, this

00:09:56.390 --> 00:10:01.610
otherwise unassuming man holds a substantial
amount of influence in the realm at the start

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:02.610
of the show.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:08.769
Who better to portray an unassuming bee lord
than experienced character actor Bill Paterson?

00:10:08.769 --> 00:10:14.010
The Scot is best known in recent times for
playing Phoebe Waller-Bridge's father in "Fleabag."

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:20.759
Of every star on this list, Paterson may have
the longest resume, as his on-screen career

00:10:20.759 --> 00:10:24.949
stretches all the way back to the early 1970s.

00:10:24.949 --> 00:10:31.480
As such, he's been a mainstay of British TV
for decades, including a brief feature on

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.006
"Doctor Who" in 2010 alongside his "House
of the Dragon" co-star Matt Smith.

